 <main><section class="world-section moon-section page-world"><div class="world-banner reveal"><div class="world-symbol moon-symbol" aria-hidden="true"></div><div><p class="eyebrow">WORLD 01 / 384,400 KM AWAY</p><h1>The Moon: <em>Footprints That Last</em></h1><p>With no wind, rain or plants to smooth its surface, the Moon keeps its traces for a very long time. Bootprints, wheel tracks and silent machines remain beneath the same unchanging sky. Here are eight stories written there.</p></div><span class="world-code">LUNA<br>01</span></div><div class="story-grid" id="moon-stories"></div></section><section class="section-wrap page-next story-handoff"><p class="eyebrow">CHAPTER 02 / THE JOURNEY CONTINUES</p><h2>From old footprints<br>to a <em>red horizon.</em></h2><p>The Moon keeps its marks. Mars gathers dust over them. Meet the robots that carried our questions farther.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="mars.html">Next chapter: Mars <span>→</span></a></section></main>
